rpi3: advertise PSCI in the device tree like the rpi4 port

The rpi3 BL31 setup only fixes up memreserve regions in the preloaded
DTB; unlike rpi4 it never adds the psci node or rewrites the cpu
enable-methods, so a kernel booted through this port keeps using
spin-tables and its CPUs can never be parked (kexec_load fails with
EBUSY, CPU hotplug is unavailable). Port the two fdt_fixup calls from
rpi4_prepare_dtb, growing the tree in place first.

The stock MAP_NS_DTB window is only 64KB; a firmware-merged tree (base
DTB + vc4/panel overlays) plus the fdt_open_into rewrite can exceed
that, and BL31 writes beyond its mapping data-abort in EL3 with the
MMU on (bench symptom: dead ACT LED, CPU parked in the exception
handler). Widen the window to 1MB to match the grow size - the DTB
sits at 16MB and the kernel at 32MB, so there is room.

